354	/*
355	 * `orderServer` — the wallet-only form action — WAS HERE, and was deleted on
356	 * 2026-07-27 along with its only caller, components/OrderForm.tsx. Read this
357	 * before writing anything that looks like it again.
358	 *
359	 * It was dead in the UI and live on the network. Nothing rendered OrderForm, but
360	 * lib/actions.ts carries `"use server"`, so `orderServer` remained a
361	 * network-callable endpoint that provisioned VMs and debited wallets — the same
362	 * property that made `verifyTotpForUser` a public 2FA oracle.
363	 *
364	 * And it was WRONG in three ways that only a second copy can be wrong:
365	 *
366	 *   1. DISPLAYED != CHARGED. OrderForm showed the plan's monthly list price as
367	 *      "Due today" while this action charged
368	 *      `promoPriceCents(vpsTermPriceCents(price, months), currentPromo(now))`.
369	 *      Under the Summer Sale an $8.99 plan displayed $8.99 and took $6.29. That
370	 *      is the 2026-07-25 incident verbatim, and it is what
371	 *      test/pricing-display-vs-charge.test.ts exists to stop.
372	 *   2. It had already DRIFTED from the real order core: no `extraDiskGB`, so it
373	 *      could neither sell nor charge for the deploy-time storage upsell that
374	 *      `orderQuote` prices.
375	 *   3. It skipped two guards `placeOrder` performs — `diskCapacityCheck`, and
376	 *      the `addons.dailyBackup` -> `autoBackup`/`backupIntervalHours` bridge
377	 *      (lib/order.ts). Every server in the live DB once carried
378	 *      `addons.dailyBackup` with `autoBackup: false` and no backup job ever
379	 *      enqueued: customers paid for backups they were never going to receive.
380	 *
381	 * `payAndDeploy` below is the one deploy path. It routes through lib/order.ts —
382	 * `intentFromFormData` + `orderQuote` + `placeOrder` — and covers BOTH the
383	 * wallet-funded and the card-funded case, so nothing was lost by removing this.
384	 * If a wallet-only form is ever wanted back, it must call `placeOrder`, not
385	 * recompose the price. One formula, one charge.
